President Trump  ran in 2016 as a populist not a  conservative and that's why he won  populism is popular at its best it's  also positive and that's what we argue  for on this show positive populism  pro-worker  pro-family pro camera themes of my book  positive populism but President Trump  needs to be careful some leading  Democrats are trying to steal his  winning populist message look at  Elizabeth Warren yes it's easy to knock  her on her dubious claim of Native  American ancestry and by the way  President Trump literally just did that  minutes ago on Twitter if you're  interested but if you listen closely  she's basically running on the Trump  message 2016 the populist bedrock of  that platform was to make government  deliver for working Americans not the  big donors and the big corporations the  focus was the middle class and working  families and now that's Elizabeth  Warren's focus to the middle class in  this country has been treated so  unfairly we will cut taxes for all  working in middle-class households in  America America's middle class is  getting hollowed out what's happening to  working families in this country why is  the path getting rockier but the echoes  go beyond the big picture look what  Warren said about Washington's  corruption when she spoke in Iowa last  week we need to change the rules in  Washington yes and it's about money in  politics it's about the influence of  money I have the biggest anti-corruption  proposals since Watergate yes  [Applause]  how about we blocked the revolving door  between Wall Street and Washington you  think I think she needs the biggest  throat lozenge to be honest anyway great  idea about the revolving door but where  have you heard that before oh right in  2016 wasn't there something about  draining the swamp fighting big money  and yes blocking the revolving door all  of that money that's going to Hillary  and Jeb and Scott and Marco and all of  them the people that are putting up that  money or it's like puppets a five-year  ban on lobbying by executive branch and  congressional officials they're not  going to be too happy a lifetime ban on  government officials lobbying for a  foreign government now it was unusual  for a Republican candidate and so was  what Donald Trump said about student  loan debt and health care we will lower  the cost of college and solve the  student loan crisis universal health  care I am going to take care of  everybody I don't care if it costs me  votes or not everybody's gonna be taking  care of much better than they're taking  care of now Wow cutting student debt  health care that takes care of everybody  that 2016 candidate sounds uncannily  similar to this 2020 candidate we pretty  much believe two-thirds three-quarters  of us want to see kids get some relief  from student loan debt want to see  affordable health care and health care  where you can't cut people out with  pre-existing conditions now I suppose  imitation is the highest form of  flattery and Warren agrees with Trump on  the need for infrastructure spending to  our roads are bad our schools are bad  our highways our tunnels our bridges our  bridges are falling down you see those  reports they're dangerous many of them  so we're going to get our infrastructure  taken care of it's going to be in jobs  but we have to do it for our country  what's happened to federal help for  infrastructure where's all that new  money that was promised for  infrastructure that would help us in  building more  that would help us in building more mass  transit that would help us in dealing  with our traffic congestion good  question what did happen to the  infrastructure plan but this political  Odd Couple even seem to agree on trade  and China I'm going to instruct my  Treasury secretary to label China a  currency manipulator the greatest in the  world any country that devalues their  currency in order to take unfair  advantage of the United States and all  of its companies who can't compete will  face tariffs and taxes to stop the  cheating they look the other way as  China manipulated its currency to  advance its own interests and undercut  work done right here in America China  has weaponized its economy without  loosening its domestic political  constraints sounds like somebody went to  Trump University look we could go on all  night but I suspect that it's quite  enough Elizabeth Warren for all of you  and we're certainly not endorsing her in  fact many of her actual policies would  be disastrous for working Americans it's  also true that many of Donald Trump's  populist promises have been delivered  top of the list of courses jobs and the  economy the poverty rate is at its  lowest point in a decade not by accident  but because of actual policy like  deregulation and tax cuts over four  million jobs have been created since  Donald Trump took office with the lowest  unemployment in half a century  and earnings rising at the fastest rate  in a decade not by chance but by  policies that boosted business  confidence and encouraged the hiring of  American workers and the clearest way of  all in which President Trump has  delivered his populist promise for  exactly the people he prioritized  manufacturing industry has boomed after  suffering for years over 400,000  manufacturing jobs have been added under  President Trump compared to a net loss  of over 200,000 under the eight years of  President Obama last year was America's  best manufacturing performance since  1997 since before China  in the World Trade Organization and  sucked all those jobs away and beyond  the economy and despite the endless  claims of the elitist establishment that  the swamp is not being trained  the President did follow through there  as well he signed an executive order  banning administration officials from  lobbying on behalf of a foreign  government and put a five-year ban on  executive branch officials lobbying the  government after they leave office but  to stop the Democrats turning populism  into their winning message in 2020  President Trump needs to reclaim the  mantle and he's got a perfect  opportunity in just a couple of weeks  time mr. president here's how you can  renew your populist revolution in your  State of the Union address with five  positive promises that will help working  Americans one on jobs fight the threat  of automation by guaranteeing retraining  for every worker who needs it that means  boosting your national council for the  American worker which helps prepare  Americans for the needs of the future  workforce under this effort led by  Ivanka Trump over a hundred companies  have promised a Reese kill a total of  over 4.3 million workers that is a great  start but you can make much more of it  to give us that massive infrastructure  program you promised make a pledge that  by 2030 America not China will have the  world's most modern systems for  transportation communication and energy  three rebuild America's struggling  neighborhoods to where the urban  suburban or rural you've already  established a White House opportunity in  revitalization Council you've got a plan  for Opportunity Zones these can be the  vehicles for a real transformation that  helps exactly the people who backed you  in 2016 for on health care you promised  to take care of everyone and then the  ideological nitwits in Congress took you  off course trust your instincts work  with Congress to deliver guaranteed  health care for every American and fifth  keep draining that swamp with a move  that every American will cheer ban  foreign government lobbying  foreign governments have embassies they  have ambassadors  why the hell should they be allowed to  use swampy lobbyists - and why the hell  should members of Congress and their  staffs be allowed to deal with them five  populous promises that will show you're  putting working Americans first  don't let elizabeth warren and the  democrats steal your winning message we  know that their brand of populism will  set the country back but mr. president  you've got to show how your version can  move America forward tell me what you  think of all that at Steve Hilton X and  that next breath  FNC

